    (596, 'Canadian Brass', '{}', 'Performer on the recordings catalogued below. See the title groups for the releases this artist appears on.', '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canadian_Brass}', 1, '2026-03-28 09:00:00.000000+00', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, DEFAULT),
    (597, 'Columbia Symphony Orchestra', '{}', 'Performer on the recordings catalogued below. See the title groups for the releases this artist appears on.', '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Columbia_Symphony_Orchestra}', 1, '2026-03-28 09:00:00.000000+00', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, DEFAULT),
    (598, 'Bruno Walter', '{}', 'Performer on the recordings catalogued below. See the title groups for the releases this artist appears on.', '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruno_Walter}', 1, '2026-03-28 09:00:00.000000+00', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, DEFAULT),
    (599, 'Cleveland Orchestra', '{}', 'Performer on the recordings catalogued below. See the title groups for the releases this artist appears on.', '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cleveland_Orchestra}', 1, '2026-03-28 09:00:00.000000+00', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, DEFAULT),
    (600, 'George Szell', '{}', 'Performer on the recordings catalogued below. See the title groups for the releases this artist appears on.', '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Szell}', 1, '2026-03-28 09:00:00.000000+00', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, DEFAULT),
    (601, 'Clark Haas', '{}', 'Clark Haas was an American comic strip artist and illustrator, best known as the creator of Clutch Cargo and, later, of Space Angel and Captain Fathom. He illustrated the Sunday edition of Buz Sawyer and ghosted Tim Tyler''s Luck for Dell, and his own short lived strip Sunnyside was distributed by Wheeler-Nicholson from 1949 to 1951. He had flown aircraft himself, which is where Clutch Cargo''s 1929 Bellanca C-27 came from.', '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clutch_Cargo}', 1, '2026-03-29 08:10:00.000000+00', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, DEFAULT),
    (602, 'Richard Cotting', '{}', 'Richard Cotting was an American radio announcer and voice actor. He spoke Clutch Cargo, the adventurer himself, and because of Syncro-Vox his mouth was filmed and optically printed onto the drawings of the character, so on screen the voice and the mouth belong to the same man.', '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clutch_Cargo}', 1, '2026-03-29 08:12:00.000000+00', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, DEFAULT),
    (603, 'Margaret Kerry', '{}', 'Margaret Kerry (born 11 November 1938) is an American actress who voiced Spinner, the freckle-faced boy who travels with Clutch Cargo, and who supplied a number of the other voices in the series. She was married to Ritchard Brown, who founded Cambria Productions.', '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clutch_Cargo}', 1, '2026-03-29 08:14:00.000000+00', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, DEFAULT),
    (604, 'Hal Smith', '{}', 'Hal Smith (3 April 1916 - 11 January 1994) was an American character actor, best known as Otis Campbell in The Andy Griffith Show. He voiced Paddlefoot, Clutch Cargo''s dachshund, and also Swampy, a character he is credited with inventing. His film work includes both of the first Star Wars films.', '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hal_Smith_(actor),https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clutch_Cargo}', 1, '2026-03-29 08:16:00.000000+00', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, DEFAULT),
    (605, 'Paul Horn', '{}', 'Paul Horn (born 17 April 1930) is an American jazz flautist and composer. He scored Clutch Cargo on bongos, vibraphone and flute.', '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Horn_(musician)}', 1, '2026-03-29 08:18:00.000000+00', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, DEFAULT),
    (606, 'Dick Brown', '{}', 'Dick Brown produced Clutch Cargo at Cambria Productions. George Bagnall and Associates sold the finished series to stations, and by the autumn of 1961 it was running on about eighty of them, reaching an estimated twenty three million viewers.', '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clutch_Cargo}', 1, '2026-03-29 08:20:00.000000+00', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, DEFAULT),
    (607, 'Edwin Gillette', '{}', 'Edwin Gillette was a television cameraman and inventor who worked with Cambria Productions. He invented Syncro-Vox, which films real human mouths and optically prints them onto drawings, having first used it on the talking animal commercials of the 1950s. Clutch Cargo was the first series built on it, and the process is still used on late night television.', '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clutch_Cargo}', 1, '2026-03-29 08:22:00.000000+00', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, DEFAULT);

-- Vivaldi, The English Concert, Simon Standage and Trevor Pinnock, whose
-- recordings of the Four Seasons make up the public domain album below. Pinnock
-- conducts from the harpsichord and Standage is the soloist, so all four are
-- credited on the title group.

--

-- Public domain authors, all of whom died in 1929 or earlier. Victor Hugo is
-- already above and his books are added to him rather than duplicated.

-- The cast and crew of the public domain cartoon series below. Clutch Cargo ran
-- for two seasons from March 1959 and is the only animated series in here: Haas
-- created it, Cotting, Kerry and Smith voiced it, Horn scored it, Brown produced
-- it and Gillette invented the Syncro-Vox process it was built on.

