    (385, NULL, 'The Complete Brandenburg Concertos Nos.1-6', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Thurston Dart, Philomusica of London recorded this for L’Oiseau‐Lyre, and it was issued as DPA 577-8 in 1977. The six concertos are the set Bach presented to Margrave Christian Ludwig of Brandenburg in 1721 as a job application he never sent. Each is scored for a different and increasingly improbable combination of instruments, and the third is the one everybody knows.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '1977-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/4db025c6-548a-42ed-9f08-47737695fda1/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Sebastian_Bach,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/033afc23-fd91-48cd-88cd-6bc28088bc11}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (386, NULL, 'The Goldberg Variations', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Glenn Gould recorded this for Sony Classical, and it was issued as SIJP-1065 in 2022. The variations are thirty keyboard pieces on an aria from the second aria of Bach''s own Italian Concerto, published in 1741 as two manuscripts with no opus number. The naming is an eighteenth century printing error: a count was misread as an opus number.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '2022-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'Japan', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/52ad72f9-b2a2-4735-9700-214dd214990a/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Sebastian_Bach,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/dcff25f1-702d-3b5e-b0da-d48172e6e62a}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (387, NULL, 'The Well-Tempered Clavier, Book 2, Preludes and Fugues 9-16', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Glenn Gould recorded this for Columbia Masterworks, and it was issued as MS 7409 in 1970. The Well-Tempered Clavier is two books of twenty four preludes and fugues, one in each of the twenty four keys, written as a tuning exercise rather than as concert music. The second book is generally held to be the later of the two.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '1970-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/4f85aada-5f9f-49b9-ba68-f7bed464fe30/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Sebastian_Bach,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/87bdaea0-dd78-4bc8-b296-57a993ef69ee}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (388, NULL, 'Eine Kleine Nachtmusik', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Amadeus Quartet, Rainer Zepperitz, Gerd Seifert, Manfred Klier recorded this for Deutsche Grammophon, and it was issued as 2531 253 in 1980. A serenade for four strings, K. 525, written in 1787 and named for its size rather than for any nocturnal programme. Its first movement is among the most played pages of chamber music ever written.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '1980-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'Germany', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/317d750a-0456-4068-9c0c-e4f202a9a2ea/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolfgang_Amadeus_Mozart,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/30bd85f2-8c53-4791-ace4-2a29a887bab4}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (389, NULL, 'Water Music', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'English Chamber Orchestra, George Malcolm recorded this for ASV, and it was issued as DCA 520 in 1983. Three orchestral suites in F major, written for a concert on the Thames in 1717 with the players in separate boats on the river. Queen Anne heard it; the King did not stay.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'English', '1983-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/04895cb0-9dc0-4d27-b052-4fe53eac26c1/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Frideric_Handel,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/5cc0cfb4-709e-4cf6-b8ca-9664f4779e15}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (390, NULL, 'Italian Concerto, BWV 971 / Fantasia, BWV 906 / Capriccio on the Departure of a Beloved Brother, BWV 992 / Chromatic Fantasia and Fugue, BWV 903 / Four Duets, BWV 802-805', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Tatiana Nikolaeva recorded this for Мелодия, and it was issued as С10 21903 005 in 1985. The release is catalogued under the numbers given above in both the Мелодия and the Olympia listings.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '1985-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'Soviet Union', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/26050946-380b-4d31-b8f9-f5f6db397e92/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Sebastian_Bach,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/f8e65a65-a625-4955-91a7-96e11cd356cb}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (391, NULL, 'Mass in B minor', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'John Eliot Gardiner recorded this for Archiv Produktion, and it was issued as 415 514 -1 in 1985. The largest work Bach wrote, assembled over some twenty five years and never performed complete in his lifetime. Its scale has often been read as a reply to the Catholic masses of the Venetians he copied out as a young man.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '1985-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'Germany', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/1db1e98a-5b64-4630-98c7-bcb71c3dee96/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Sebastian_Bach,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/9ff5f872-d22b-3dc7-a50e-dcba22248a51}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (392, NULL, 'St. Matthew Passion', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'The Bach Choir, David Willcocks recorded this for Decca Records, and it was issued as D139D 4 in 1979. Performed in the Church of St Thomas in Leipzig in 1727 or 1728 and revised for 1729. Bach provided four performing forces, four organs and a full complement of instruments and continuo for a text which is very nearly all Gospel.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '1979-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/f00a3ec9-b88d-4720-9f27-9c4cfa684ad5/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Sebastian_Bach,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/37e55808-1146-47f3-95c7-baea87ec9e19}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (393, NULL, 'Requiem', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'The New Siberian Singers, MusicAeterna, Teodor Currentzis recorded this for Alpha Classics, and it was issued as ALPHA 468 in 2019. Mozart''s last work, left incomplete at his death, with a note in the autograph asking the copyist to leave the lacunae marked. Süssmayr and later hands supplied the missing movements.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '2019-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'France', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/1a1260d1-ccee-4d71-8b09-47c799ea978c/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolfgang_Amadeus_Mozart,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/2d1cdc4e-b3e5-4898-8dad-7c7bf4e5a29f}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (394, NULL, 'Symphony no. 7 / Coriolan Overture / Egmont Overture', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Philharmonia Orchestra, Vladimir Ashkenazy recorded this for Decca Records, and it was issued as 411 941-1 in 1984. The works of Beethoven''s late twenties, written as he was beginning to go deaf and on the edge of the French Revolution.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '1984-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/0f36f31a-5443-4190-947e-32ae63e7e96b/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ludwig_van_Beethoven,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/1abbb4ed-89d9-4054-ab2a-4f37a601c4df}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (395, NULL, 'The Complete Piano Sonatas', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Alfred Brendel recorded this for Philips, and it was issued as 6768 004 in 1978. Thirty two sonatas spanning the whole career, from the Op. 2 set of the 1790s to the last three of 1822, and the largest body of keyboard music written before the twentieth century.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '1978-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'Netherlands', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/3485f032-567a-4fa4-ad55-390dc1d0e0a6/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ludwig_van_Beethoven,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/23cfddb8-89c4-3675-9590-0f1fa6c14db1}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (396, NULL, 'Six Flute Concertos, op. 10', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Stephen Preston (flautist), Academy of Ancient Music, Christopher Hogwood recorded this for L’Oiseau‐Lyre, and it was issued as DSLO 519 in 1977. Vivaldi''s first published set of flute concertos, issued in Venice around 1728 and, unlike most of his concertos, written for one soloist.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'Italian', '1977-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/6413d746-e8d8-4ead-8047-523faa1a3269/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antonio_Vivaldi,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/3ea84651-6eaa-4537-87de-010bd1437d51}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (397, NULL, 'Le Quattro Stagioni', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Felix Ayo, I Musici recorded this for Philips, and it was issued as SABL 117 in 1959. The Four Seasons are the first four concerti of Op. 8, each a three movement work illustrating a sonnet printed alongside it.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'Italian', '1959-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/51e7ef36-5871-4b7f-8a8a-9344d4dd853a/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antonio_Vivaldi,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/2cc0c352-bd18-407c-8ef1-436a24ed8482}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (398, NULL, 'Great Mass in C minor', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Sylvia McNair, Diana Montague, Anthony Rolfe Johnson, Cornelius Hauptmann, Monteverdi Choir, English Baroque Soloists, John Eliot Gardiner recorded this for Philips, and it was issued as 420 210-1 in 1987. Mozart''s setting of the Benedictus from the mass ordinary, begun in 1783 and finished eleven years later, immediately before the Requiem.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '1987-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'Netherlands', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/9b2c3282-0272-44da-b455-f95e04f4a85c/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolfgang_Amadeus_Mozart,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/19be0088-a13f-4202-8629-ccf2fe35f9fb}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (399, NULL, 'Symphonien Nr. 5 & 8', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Herbert von Karajan, Berlin Philharmonic recorded this for Deutsche Grammophon, and it was issued as 419 051-1 in 1986. The Fifth and the Eighth, the two Beethoven symphonies most often coupled, sit either side of his deafness and of his change of manner.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '1986-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'Germany', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/06b7f1e4-577a-421e-bf78-db3d33c7bc79/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ludwig_van_Beethoven,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/2dc50fd2-4b8f-4d60-a648-01564358980a}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (400, NULL, 'Toccata & Fugue in D minor / Prelude & Fugue in E-flat / Prelude, Largo & Fugue in C', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Daniel Chorzempa recorded this for Philips, and it was issued as 6514 274 in 1982. The release is catalogued under the numbers given above in both the Philips and the Philips listings.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '1982-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'Netherlands', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/56739005-a3c3-45e0-ba78-43a5292fd050/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Sebastian_Bach,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/57a3e4c6-819b-314b-a1e1-4f0347a5c211}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (401, NULL, 'Messiah: A Sacred Oratorio (highlights)', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Academy of Ancient Music, Christ Church Cathedral Choir, Oxford, Christopher Hogwood recorded this for L’Oiseau‐Lyre, and it was issued as DSLO 592 in 1981. An oratorio on a libretto by Charles Jennens compiled from the King James Bible. Handel conducted the Dublin premiere in 1742 and, told the audience would not be let out during a Hallelujah, asked for the doors to be locked.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'English', '1981-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/9d5deb35-9f7f-4d50-a381-d0fcbd42feb4/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Frideric_Handel,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/60d4c2c4-5ea3-4f5e-8099-46ec9127bc0b}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (402, NULL, 'The Pachelbel Canon: The Canadian Brass Plays Great Baroque Music', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Canadian Brass recorded this for RCA Red Seal, and it was issued as ARL1-3554 in 1980. The release is catalogued under the numbers given above in both the RCA Red Seal and the RCA Red Seal listings.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '1980-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'Germany', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/fb994fbb-2ef1-4ad3-b99d-409406403eb4/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Pachelbel,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/44d00002-df78-39b9-8129-0bf72cf313cd}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (403, NULL, 'Symphonies 1 & 2', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Columbia Symphony Orchestra, Bruno Walter recorded this for Philips, and it was issued as 835540LY in 1959. Written while Beethoven was still in his twenties and squarely in the high classical manner of Haydn and Mozart.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '1959-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'United Kingdom', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/27b2dee9-5a06-49bf-9e44-fb7bc00b95a2/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ludwig_van_Beethoven,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/23625408-c674-4501-93c0-8050fb1ed522}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (404, NULL, 'Serenades: Eine kleine Nachtmusik, K. 525 / "Posthorn" Serenade (no. 9 in D major), K. 320', '{}', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', '2026-03-28 08:00:00.000000+00', 1, E'Cleveland Orchestra, George Szell recorded this for Columbia Masterworks, and it was issued as MS 7273 in 1973. The release is catalogued under the numbers given above in both the Columbia Masterworks and the CBS/Sony listings.\n\nThe music is in the public domain. The recording, and the tapes and pressings behind it, are not.', NULL, 'German', '1973-01-01 00:00:00+00', TRUE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://coverartarchive.org/release/ee16c991-6755-4f32-a942-36de380907ee/front-500}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wolfgang_Amadeus_Mozart,https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/02d30471-63aa-33d5-9813-aca9fb54b17f}', '{}', 'Album', 'music', '{}', '{}', NULL),
    (405, NULL, 'Season 1', '{}', '2026-03-29 08:05:00.000000+00', '2026-03-29 08:05:00.000000+00', 1, E'The first twenty-six of the fifty-two Clutch Cargo stories, broadcast weekly from 14 March to 5 September 1959. Each show is half an hour and is assembled from five five-minute chapters, the first four of which ended on a cliffhanger so that a station could run one chapter a day through the week and recap the whole at the weekend.

Every show is one entry in the logbook of the same name. The Friendly Head Hunters opens the run on 14 March 1959 and Space Station closes it on 5 September 1959, after which the series was off the air for six months.

The picture is a 16mm print with Syncro-Vox lips over still drawings, scored by Paul Horn on bongos, vibraphone and flute. Nothing in this season was ever registered for copyright in the United States.', NULL, 'English', '1959-03-14 00:00:00+00', FALSE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/v4/season/573391/posters/6359ac8beef22.jpg}', '{https://thetvdb.com/series/clutch-cargo/seasons/official/1}', '{}', NULL, 'tv_show', '{}', '{}', 9),
    (406, NULL, 'Season 2', '{}', '2026-03-29 08:06:00.000000+00', '2026-03-29 08:06:00.000000+00', 1, E'The second twenty-six stories, broadcast weekly from 12 March to 3 September 1960, completing the run at fifty-two. The Swamp Swindlers opens on 12 March 1960 and Big ''X'' closes the series on 3 September 1960.

The format is the first season''s unchanged: five five-minute chapters a show, four of them ending on a cliffhanger. The chapter structure is most visible here, because these are the shows stations actually ran on a Saturday morning and the weekday airings were recaps cut from them.

Same 16mm prints, same Syncro-Vox, same public domain.', NULL, 'English', '1960-03-12 00:00:00+00', FALSE, NULL, 'United States', '{https://artworks.thetvdb.com/banners/v4/season/1806190/posters/64cca987b2b85.jpg}', '{https://thetvdb.com/series/clutch-cargo/seasons/official/2}', '{}', NULL, 'tv_show', '{}', '{}', 9),
    (407,NULL,'Season 1','{}','2026-04-01 08:30:00+00','2026-04-01 08:30:00+00',1,E'The original Star Trek, five seasons of commission aboard a starship that was cancelled after three. Never renewed, so it has been in the public domain in the United States since the copyright lapsed, and it is the most redistributed television programme ever made.

