    (1136, 405, NULL, '2005-03-22', FALSE, '2026-03-29 08:40:00.000000+00', '2026-03-29 08:40:00.000000+00', 1, 'The first of the two DVDs, holding the whole of the first season in standard definition. Alongside the twenty-six shows it carries The Story of Clutch Cargo, Clutch Memorabilia, Clutch & Company, a set of mini biographies of the cast, a 1959 facts and trivia reel, and a bonus Syncro-Vox cartoon that is not one of the fifty-two. Released with Volume 2 on the same day.', NULL, '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clutch_Cargo}', 'DVD', '{}'),
    (1137, 405, NULL, NULL, FALSE, '2026-03-29 08:41:00.000000+00', '2026-03-29 08:41:00.000000+00', 1, 'The digital transfer the archive.org upload is made from, which in turn was made from these DVDs. The collection is undated and holds twenty-four of the fifty-two shows under an uploader''s own naming, so it is the least complete of the three sources and the only one carrying no subtitles of its own.', NULL, '{}', '{https://archive.org/details/clutchcargocartooonscollection,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clutch_Cargo}', 'Web', '{}'),
    (1138, 405, NULL, '1959-03-14', FALSE, '2026-03-29 08:42:00.000000+00', '2026-03-29 08:42:00.000000+00', 1, 'The original release, as it went out: a 16mm print, in black and white or in colour as it had been filmed, licensed station to station by George Bagnall and Associates and rebroadcast for a decade afterwards. No master of these prints survives, which is why nearly everything circulating comes either from the DVDs or from off air recordings of them.', NULL, '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clutch_Cargo}', 'TV', '{}'),
    (1139, 406, NULL, '2005-03-22', FALSE, '2026-03-29 08:43:00.000000+00', '2026-03-29 08:43:00.000000+00', 1, 'The second of the two DVDs, holding the whole of the second season. Its extras are The Making of Clutch Cargo, Politically Incorrect, As Seen in Pulp Fiction, a reel of 1959 trailers and a bonus Syncro-Vox cartoon. Released with Volume 1 on the same day.', NULL, '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clutch_Cargo}', 'DVD', '{}'),
    (1140, 406, NULL, NULL, FALSE, '2026-03-29 08:44:00.000000+00', '2026-03-29 08:44:00.000000+00', 1, 'The digital transfer the archive.org upload is made from, which in turn was made from these DVDs. The collection is undated and holds twenty-four of the fifty-two shows under an uploader''s own naming, so it is the least complete of the three sources and the only one carrying no subtitles of its own.', NULL, '{}', '{https://archive.org/details/clutchcargocartooonscollection,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clutch_Cargo}', 'Web', '{}'),
    (1141, 406, NULL, '1960-03-12', FALSE, '2026-03-29 08:45:00.000000+00', '2026-03-29 08:45:00.000000+00', 1, 'The original release, as it went out: a 16mm print, in black and white or in colour as it had been filmed, licensed station to station by George Bagnall and Associates and rebroadcast for a decade afterwards. No master of these prints survives, which is why nearly everything circulating comes either from the DVDs or from off air recordings of them.', NULL, '{}', '{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clutch_Cargo}', 'TV', '{}'),
