--

-- Torrents for the book editions above. Ebooks ship as an EPUB and a PDF, audiobooks
-- as an M4B and a split MP3.
--
-- Torrents for the Night of the Living Dead editions above: encodes, remuxes and web
-- rips. Five per resolution tier: a large encode for fidelity, a compact one for
-- seeding ratio, a full disc rip, a web rip and the one release carrying the extras,
-- plus full disc rips of the 3D disc and the DVD. Regular releases are a single
-- file with no folder and no nfo; only the full disc rips get a folder and an nfo.
-- The Criterion 4K UHD disc is SDR, so the HDR10 grades are illustrative.
--
-- Torrents for the Four Seasons editions above: four per edition, a 24/96 FLAC, a
-- 16/44.1 FLAC and the two MP3s. Rips are split one file per movement with a cue
-- sheet, and the physical editions also carry a cover and an nfo. The vinyl and
-- cassette rips are upsampled to 24 bit for the hi-res encode, which is what a
-- scene release would do rather than leave the format at 16/44.1.
--
-- The CD and the German LP both come with a four language insert, but the scans
-- are their own release rather than part of the album, so each of those two
-- editions gets a single extras torrent holding just the scans and nothing of the
-- music. The LP is given the record and label scans on top of the insert. The US
-- club edition is a plain cardboard sleeve and the cassette is a shell, so neither
-- has anything worth scanning.

--
-- Torrents for the Clutch Cargo seasons above, seven a season. The DVD gets a full
-- disc rip, an encode of that disc kept for the seeding ratio, and the five extras
-- the discs came with; the web edition gets the full size transfer and a half
-- size of it; the TV edition gets the two captures a public domain season usually
-- turns up, one off a station rebroadcast and one off a satellite feed. The disc
-- rips are the only releases here that are not a file per episode, and the captures
-- are the only ones left interlaced.

